WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.520
Speaker 1: I want to talk today about one tool&nbsp;
used by reactionaries to fool people and to goad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:14.480
people into reactionary beliefs, and that is the&nbsp;
use of the fake or or imaginary slippery slope.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:22.960
In general, reactionaries use fear as a tool.&nbsp;
They aggrandize threats beyond what they are to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:28.720
make people afraid, and then they use that fear&nbsp;
to try to get people to support certain policies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:36.080
If you're really afraid of brown people from&nbsp;
Mexico coming to commit crimes and take your jobs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:42.560
you're likely to support extreme policies&nbsp;
on immigration. So the use of fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:49.680
and fearmongering by reactionaries is very&nbsp;
common. One example of the false slippery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:56.480
slope and a slippery slope is saying, Well, if we&nbsp;
do a, it's definitively going to lead to B, C, D,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:04.000
e f, etc. When sometimes a will just be a an.&nbsp;
A great example we have because of the pandemic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.000
is the fake slippery slope of vaccine&nbsp;
mandates. As you may know, for over a year now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.120
the reactionary right has been saying the first&nbsp;
thing is you've got to get a COVID vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:22.880
and the next thing you know, ABCD EFG.&nbsp;
And we now have over 200 years of history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.320
to tell us that vaccine mandates don't lend&nbsp;
themselves to more authoritarianism. And you just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:34.400
look at the history. And 1777 George Washington&nbsp;
required the smallpox vaccine for all soldiers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.800
And then, you know, 30 years went by, and in&nbsp;
18 09, Massachusetts put in its first vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.080
mandate. And then another 40 years went by and&nbsp;
then in 1855, a Massachusetts, Massachusetts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:53.600
instituted vaccine requirements for schools. And&nbsp;
then in 1985, in the U.S. Supreme Court case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.040
Jacobson v. Massachusetts, the Supreme Court&nbsp;
said now municipalities can. This can can put in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:05.040
a vaccine mandate. And people were saying, this is&nbsp;
the start of what? And it just never went further.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.680
In 1977, we had the childhood immunization&nbsp;
initiative start, and it's just about getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.640
kids vaccinated. And more recently, people with&nbsp;
the COVID vaccine saying this is the start of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.560
dystopian authority now. And in fact, many places&nbsp;
have already removed vaccine mandates for travel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.640
Employers are removing vaccine mandates as the&nbsp;
pandemic wanes, and so it's an obviously false&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:32.400
slippery slope. The vaccine mandates over the last&nbsp;
200 years have not led to anything more than that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:40.800
You can really tell the difference in how the&nbsp;
right uses slippery slopes and fearmongering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:44.320
by thinking about something like health&nbsp;
care. I mean, look, I just think it through.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:51.600
We on the left say about health care. Listen, the&nbsp;
right wants this like total for profit free market&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:57.440
health care thing. They generally speaking, want&nbsp;
to let insurance companies charge whatever they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:03.360
want to. People with preexisting conditions deny&nbsp;
them insurance. And if the right got its way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.760
we would continue to see medical bankruptcies,&nbsp;
which we're already seeing. We would continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:13.120
to see people unable to afford or access care,&nbsp;
which we already see. All of this stuff exists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:19.360
right now. There's no crazy fear mongering&nbsp;
from the left on health insurance, the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:27.040
says. If the left gets his way gets its way. It's&nbsp;
the start of a communist takeover of health care,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.160
where government bureaucrats will create death&nbsp;
panels and decide whether you live or die.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:40.000
And it will be the start of a government takeover&nbsp;
of every industry. What so you see how one side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:46.160
does the slippery slope, reactionary fear&nbsp;
mongering? And we say we're going to continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:51.920
seeing the same problems. If we don't, if we don't&nbsp;
fix this very different language that's used.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:57.600
So the best thing when you start hearing these&nbsp;
slippery slope claims, if you do this, it's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:03.600
to lead to all this other stuff. First of all, ask&nbsp;
for examples of when that has happened, that one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:11.280
tool that you can use. Secondly, ask the person&nbsp;
claiming the slippery slope will happen to explain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.800
exactly how. Because if you actually say to&nbsp;
people, well, hold on. How will a vaccine mandate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.760
on COVID vaccines lead to whatever it is you're&nbsp;
afraid of? Like exactly what are the steps and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:28.800
who will enact it? And it's also a good tool to&nbsp;
show the disconnect between the different pieces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:34.480
of this slippery slope. Often, they won't even&nbsp;
explain the path down the slope. When they do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:39.440
it often makes no sense whatsoever. So those are&nbsp;
some tools that you can use. But whenever you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:44.800
presented with a slippery slope, ask yourselves&nbsp;
those questions. Is there historical evidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:50.320
that that's what would actually happen? How would&nbsp;
it happen? And does that actually make any sense?

